Rina (Docs): Quick ask  drafting a tiny migration note for v1->v2 embeddings. Need a copy-paste TS + curl example using model_id, the exact short error text for dim mismatch, and a one-line changelog blurb for the banner. Keep it minimal for localization.

Kevin (SDK): TS snippet you can paste:
```ts
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk';
const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RDW_KEY });
const alias = { 'embed-old-512':'embed-new-768' };
const model_id = alias['embed-old-512'] ?? 'embed-old-512';
const r = await c.embeddings.create({ model_id, input: ['hi'] });
console.log(r.data[0].embedding.length);
```
Curl one-liner: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v2/embeddings -H "Authorization: Bearer $RDW_KEY" -d '{"model_id":"embed-new-768","input":["x"]}'`

Alex (Runtime): Exact trimmed error: `{"error":"embedding failed: vector_dim 512 != expected 768","code":"ERR_DIM_MISMATCH"}`. Use the fragment "embedding failed: vector_dim" in troubleshooting copy. Also recommend pinning model versions for deterministic vectors during rollouts.

Sam (PM): Changelog blurb suggestion (1 line): "Embeddings: param rename to model_id (model alias supported); ERR_DIM_MISMATCH on dim mismatch. See migration quickstart."

Priya (L10n): That sentence is fine for translation if kept as a single short line in the PR.

Rina (Docs): Thanks — action items: Kevin add snippet + changelog to SDK PR, Alex add small test that asserts the 400 contains "vector_dim", Priya queue L10n on merge, Rina will add TS + curl + one-line troubleshooting to docs PR and merge when green. :thumbsup:

(End)
